# AI-Native Game Boy

## MVP Project Requirements & Cursor Agent Work Packages

### 0. Project Objective

Build a playable 2D top-down, Game Boy-inspired monster-catching game running on an Arduino UNO Q with:

* Arduino Modulino Joystick
* Arduino Modulino 3 Button
* Waveshare display
* UNO Q provided hardware/software stack
* Summer Engine
* Summer MCP
* GitHub shared repository
* Cursor AI coding agents

The MVP should reproduce the feeling of exploring a small classic handheld monster-catching game:

1. Start the game.
2. Navigate a top-down grassland world.
3. Control a player character.
4. Explore the environment.
5. Encounter creatures at a defined spawn rate.
6. Enter a battle.
7. Fight the creature.
8. Attempt to catch it.
9. Return to the overworld.
10. Open the menu.
11. View equipped/owned creatures and inventory.

The first biome is **grassland only**.

The MVP must prioritize:

**playability > integration > game feel > visual polish > additional features.**

Do not add features outside this specification until the MVP is fully playable.

