# 3. Git Rules

Every developer works on their own branch.

Recommended branches:

```text
main

feature/core
feature/world
feature/encounters
feature/battle
feature/catching
feature/ui
```

Rules:

* Never directly rewrite another developer's system.
* Never commit generated junk/build directories.
* Do not rename shared files without notifying the integration owner.
* Pull from `main` frequently.
* Keep commits small and descriptive.
* Each feature must be independently testable.
* Merge only after the feature works.

Commit examples:

```text
feat: add player movement
feat: add grassland collision
feat: implement random encounters
feat: implement battle state
feat: add creature inventory
feat: add menu navigation
fix: prevent player movement during battle
```

