# 11. Hardware Integration Contract

The hardware developer is intentionally **not assigned a separate workstream**.

The hardware is treated as plug-and-play.

The rest of the team should therefore program against:

```text
INPUT
```

rather than:

```text
JOYSTICK HARDWARE
```

The physical controls should map approximately to:

```text
Joystick up       → UP
Joystick down     → DOWN
Joystick left     → LEFT
Joystick right    → RIGHT

Button 1          → CONFIRM / ACTION
Button 2          → BACK / CANCEL
Button 3          → MENU
```

The exact mapping can be changed centrally.

No game system should care whether input comes from:

* UNO Q
* keyboard
* joystick
* automated testing

This allows the team to develop rapidly on PCs and then run on the hardware.

