The following events should be standardized:

```text
PLAYER_MOVED
ENCOUNTER_TRIGGERED

BATTLE_STARTED
BATTLE_WON
BATTLE_LOST
BATTLE_ESCAPED

CATCH_STARTED
CREATURE_CAUGHT
CATCH_FAILED

MENU_OPENED
MENU_CLOSED

INVENTORY_CHANGED
PARTY_CHANGED
ACTIVE_CREATURE_CHANGED
```

This is extremely important.

For example:

**World developer:**

```text
PLAYER_MOVED
```

↓

**Encounter developer:**

```text
check encounter
```

↓

```text
ENCOUNTER_TRIGGERED
```

↓

**Core:**

```text
OVERWORLD → BATTLE
```

↓

**Battle developer:**

```text
BATTLE_STARTED
```

This prevents six agents from tightly coupling their code.

